  "configuration_id": "config_043",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_031, scvi_n200/resnet50/avgpool/weighted/multiprofile, acc=0.678) shows that RNA encoder choice is a high-impact design decision (scvi_n200 gave +4 pts over pca_n2000). However, scgpt—a fundamentally different pre-trained single-cell encoder (generative vs. variational vs. linear PCA)—has zero experimental evidence. Meanwhile, the image encoder axis (resnet50 vs. imagenet_vit_l) showed negligible difference (~0.4 pts) with pca_n2000, making further image-encoder exploration lower-value. Question: config_043 (scgpt, resnet50, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) directly compares scgpt against scvi_n200 in an otherwise identical, best-performing setup, isolating the RNA encoder effect. Why best next experiment: It resolves the largest remaining uncertainty (which RNA encoder is optimal) with a single experiment, and the answer will guide all subsequent multimodal configurations. If scgpt matches or beats scvi_n200, it opens a new promising direction; if it underperforms, we confirm scvi_n200 as the best encoder and can focus remaining budget on finer-tuning aggregation/fusion interactions."
}

